          "**noise_std** (float) – The standard deviation of the noise injected into the model input for engression.",
          "**noise_type** (str) – The type of noise injected into the model input for engression.",
          "**num_samples** (int) – The number of samples drawn from the noise distribution at prediction time for engression.",
          "**input_chunk_length** (int) – Number of past time steps that are fed to the forecasting module at prediction time.",
          "**model** (str | type[CustomRNNModule]) – Either a string specifying the EnRNN (Engression-enhanced RNN) module type (“EnRNN (Engression-enhanced RNN)”, “LSTM” or “GRU”), or a subclass of CustomRNNModule (the class itself, not an object of the class) with a custom logic.",
          "**hidden_dim** (int) – Size for feature maps for each hidden EnRNN (Engression-enhanced RNN) layer (\\(h_n\\)).",
          "**n_rnn_layers** (int) – The number of recurrent layers.",
          "**dropout** (float) – Fraction of neurons affected by Dropout.",
          "**training_length** (int) – The length of both input (target and covariates) and output (target) time series used during training. Must be >input_chunk_length, because otherwise during training the EnRNN (Engression-enhanced RNN) is never run for as many iterations as it will during inference. For training, a ShiftedTorchTrainingDataset is used with parameters input_chunk_length=output_chunk_length=training_length and shift=1.",
